<title>POLAND: BANK HANDLOWY SELLS FORD, POLISH AIRCRAFT MAKER CPS.</title>
<headline>BANK HANDLOWY SELLS FORD, POLISH AIRCRAFT MAKER CPS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Bank Handlowy sold six million zlotys of commercial papers for Ford Credit Europe plc, a unit of Ford Motor Co., and 16.6 million zlotys of CP's for Polish aircraft maker, WSK PZL Swidnik SA, the bank said.</p>
<p>It said in a statement Ford Credit Europe's paper, which matures on October 14, 1996, was sold with an a maximum yield of 18.52 percent. The average yield was also 18.52 percent.</p>
<p>The state-owned aircraft maker's paper, which matures on October 15, 1996, was sold with an maximum yield of 19.01 percent and an average yield of 18.93 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
